--- !u!114 &644053940
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 644053937}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Controls:

    \tWASD - Move

    \tMouse - Look Around

    \tSpace -
    Jump

    \tE - Interact

    \tLeft Click - Use Item

    \tEscape - Pause




    How
    To Play:

    To win complete 20 days without your family or your community starving.
    Harvest crops and sell them to your community at the market or store them in
    the box by your house for your family.


    To plant a crop till the soil with
    a hoe, use a seed packet to plant then make sure to water it every day. Use the
    watering can to water them which can be filled by interacting with the green
    water tank. Seeds can be bought from the market


    Every day if the crop is
    watered it will move to the next stage. Crops don''t need to be watered if there
    is rain. Soil is darker if it is wet. Rain also fills up the water tank.  If
    there is no rain you can always buy water for your tank.


    To move to the
    next day interact with the door to your house but make sure everyone has enough
    food before proceeding.




    Drought Disaster:

    Sometimes droughts happen,
    during these rain won''t appear for a while. Certain crops also will require
    more water so make sure to check if their soil is darker. Use water wisely.


    Pest
    Disaster:

    Sometimes pests will attack your crops. To kill them use BT spray.
    To reduce the chance of them attacking a crop use neem oil. Both of these can
    be bought from the shop. Pests do glow slightly so keep an eye out.




    Seasons:

    The
    game has 4 seasons, all of them affect the chance of rain and disasters. Also
    everyone will need different amounts of food every day depending on the season.




    Crop
    Information:

    \tCowpea - Green seed packet. Harvest on stage 3 or 4 (green/yellow
    pods)

    \tSorghum - Yellow seed packet. Harvest on stage 3 (yellow grains)

    \tTomato
    - Red Packet. Harvest on stage 5 (red fruits)'
